+---
+name: mornica-spotify-grade-upgrade
+description: Upgrade the Moronto Mornica native Android app (Kotlin/Jetpack Compose/Material 3/Media3; GitHub SHADOWSPARK-TECHNOLOGIES/Moronto-music-app) toward a Spotify-grade information architecture — home feed shelves, search, playlists with reorder, downloads screen, settings, enhanced now-playing with queue + sleep timer, on-device recommendations — using drop-in Compose/Kotlin templates that integrate with the existing PlaybackRouter, MornicaRuntime, and rights-gate architecture. Use when the user asks to make the music app "Spotify-like", add home/search/playlist/download/settings/queue features, improve the player UX, build a feature-upgrade contract for Hermes, or plan the next development phase of Mornica. Enforces the repo's default-deny rights gate, YouTube ToS boundary, and Play Store policy guardrails; never bypasses compliance.
+---
+
+# Mornica — Spotify-grade feature upgrade (templates + execution workflow)
+
+## Purpose
+
+Raise Mornica from a working offline player + demo catalog to a Spotify-grade **information architecture and interaction model** (shelves, search, playlists, downloads, queue, settings, recommendations) while keeping Mornica's own Midnight Slate / Jade / Amber brand system. This skill copies **patterns and ergonomics**, not Spotify branding, colors, assets, or code.
+
+Target repo: `SHADOWSPARK-TECHNOLOGIES/Moronto-music-app`, package `com.shadowspark.morontomornica`, Kotlin 2.2.10, Compose BOM, Media3 1.5.1, minSdk 26 / targetSdk 36.
+
+## Hard guardrails (from repo AGENTS.md — non-negotiable, never "bypassed")
+
+1. `LicensedCatalogRights.evaluate(track, CatalogAccess.*, territory)` runs **before any MediaItem reaches ExoPlayer**. Default-deny. No new playback path skips it.
+2. Never allow `youtube.com` / `youtu.be` / `googlevideo.com` URIs into the Media3 player. No stream extraction, ripping, or YouTube audio downloads. YouTube remains an external, clearly-labeled discovery surface only.
+3. Demo fixtures stay visibly labeled `DEMO` with `licenseReference = DEMO-*`. Never fabricate `rightsConfirmed = true` for a track without an authenticated backend agreement.
+4. No push, merge, release signing, Play Console mutation, or deployment without explicit human approval. This skill builds code and verifies locally only.
+5. No surprise dependencies, permissions, global config, or backend changes. New dependencies (Room, Coil, lifecycle-viewmodel-compose, media3-ui) exist only as commented snippets under `assets/templates/config/` and require owner approval before wiring.
+6. Preserve every existing test. After each phase the gates below must stay green; never delete or weaken an existing test.
+7. Report results separately: **unit-verified / build-verified / device-verified / unverified**. No self-asserted success; two failures on the same cause → stop, preserve exact errors, propose fix, wait.
+
+## Architecture invariants (reuse, don't replace)
+
+- State source of truth: `domain/PlaybackRouter.kt` exposing `state: StateFlow<MornicaUiState>`. New screens consume `uiState` + call router methods; do not fork a second state holder.
+- Wiring singleton: `domain/MornicaRuntime.kt` (router, localRepo, youtubeRepo, download wiring). New repositories attach there, idempotently, from `MainActivity.onCreate`.
+- Player engine: `LocalAudioController` / `Media3LocalAudioController` + `LocalAudioPlaybackService` (Media3 `MediaSessionService`). New transport calls go through the router/controller interface; never instantiate a second ExoPlayer.
+- Catalog downloads: `CatalogDownloadManager` / `CatalogDownloadService` / `DownloadStore` JSON seam; `OfflineReadinessVerifier` gates "Ready offline" on real Media3 `DownloadIndex` bytes.
+- Brand tokens: `ui/MornicaTheme.kt` (`MornicaEmerald`, `MornicaCyan`, `MornicaAmber*`, `MornicaSlate*`, `MornicaTokens`). New UI imports these; do not define competing color sets.
+
+## Install in the repo
+
+Copy this whole folder into the repo at `.agents/skills/mornica-spotify-grade-upgrade/` (sibling of the existing `.agents/skills/mornica-*` skills) so Hermes and other repo agents discover it. `scripts/verify.sh` locates the repo root automatically from that location.
+
+## Template rules
+
+1. Templates under `assets/templates/` are **additive new files**. Place each at its target path from `references/integration-map.md`.
+2. Existing files (`MornicaApp.kt`, `MainActivity.kt`, `MornicaRuntime`, build files) are changed only via the minimal patches in `assets/templates/patches/existing-file-patches.md` — small, reversible diffs.
+3. Phase A/B templates use only existing dependencies (Compose, Material3, coroutines, media3, org.json on-device). Phase C/D optional deps stay behind the config snippets until approved.
+4. Pure-Kotlin logic (recommender, playlist store interface, shelf models) is framework-free so it runs under JUnit + Robolectric like the existing suite.
+
+## Execution workflow
+
+Read `references/phased-plan.md` first. Run one phase at a time:
+
+1. Sync: `git fetch origin && git checkout main && git pull origin main`, then branch `feat/mornica-spotify-phase<N>-<slug>`.
+2. Copy the phase's template files to the target paths; apply the listed patches.
+3. Run gates (`scripts/verify.sh`):
+   - `./gradlew :app:testDebugUnitTest` — existing tests stay green plus new phase tests.
+   - `./gradlew :app:lintDebug` — 0 errors.
+   - `./gradlew :app:assembleDebug` — debug APK builds.
+   - When touching playback: `./gradlew :app:connectedDebugAndroidTest -Pandroid.testInstrumentationRunnerArguments.class=com.shadowspark.morontomornica.LicensedCatalogPlaybackInstrumentedTest`.
+4. Conventional commits: `feat(mornica-spotify): …`, `test(mornica-spotify): …`, `refactor(mornica-spotify): …`.
+5. Update `docs/agent-loop/STATE.md` and `docs/EXECUTION_LOG.md` with unit/build/device/unverified labels before opening a PR.
+6. PR targets `main`, uses `.github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md`, lists gates per verified category. No merge without owner approval.
+
+## Resource map
+
+- `references/feature-matrix.md` — Spotify-equivalent feature → Mornica today → target → template file → phase.
+- `references/integration-map.md` — every template: source path, target path, existing symbols used, new symbols, required approval.
+- `references/phased-plan.md` — phases A–D scope, acceptance criteria, gates, owner approvals.
+- `references/data-source-contract.md` — specialized licensed-catalog data source contract (backend seam, schema, signed URLs, rights gate, NG region).
+- `assets/templates/core/` — pure logic: recommender, sleep timer, route holder.
+- `assets/templates/data/` — playlist persistence seam (JSON now, Room-ready interface).
+- `assets/templates/ui/` — Compose screens and components.
+- `assets/templates/tests/` — new unit tests matching existing package/style.
+- `assets/templates/config/` — dependency/manifest snippets (approval-gated, not applied automatically).
+- `assets/templates/patches/existing-file-patches.md` — minimal diffs to existing files.
+- `assets/ai-studio/` — paste-ready prompts for Google AI Studio when the repo is imported there: `00-sync-prompt.md` first, then `02`–`05` per phase; `01-output-protocol.md` governs file-path-delimited Kotlin output. AI Studio cannot run Gradle, so gates stay local (`scripts/verify.sh`); every unverified claim is labeled.
+- `scripts/verify.sh` — run the three local gates; `scripts/template_consistency_check.sh` — package/path and guardrail-token consistency over templates.
+
+## Definition of done (per phase)
+
+- All template files at target paths; patches applied; existing tests untouched and green.
+- New tests green; lint 0 errors; debug APK builds.
+- UI changes checked on emulator; screenshots + uiautomator tree recorded in `docs/EXECUTION_LOG.md` per existing evidence practice.
+- No new permission, dependency, network call, or rights claim without an explicit owner-approval note in the commit message and PR body.
