+# Specialized catalog data-source contract (Mornica licensed catalogue)
+
+Purpose: define the production data source that replaces demo fixtures without weakening the default-deny rights gate. Implements the existing `CatalogSource` seam in `domain/LicensedCatalogRepository.kt`; it does not replace it.
+
+## Existing seam (do not redesign)
+
+```kotlin
+interface CatalogSource {
+  val label: String
+  val isDemo: Boolean
+  fun tracks(): List<LicensedCatalogTrack>
+  fun byId(id: String): LicensedCatalogTrack?
+}
+```
+
+`LicensedCatalogBackendSource` currently returns `emptyList()` (fail-closed). The backend implementation fills it once real agreements exist; `LicensedCatalogRights.evaluate(...)` stays in front of every playback/download decision.
+
+## Source requirements (specialized for Mornica)
+
+1. **Metadata store**: Firestore (or equivalent document store), region `africa-south1` (Johannesburg) for lowest Nigeria latency; collections:
+   - `tracks/{trackId}`: `title, artist, album, genre, releaseYear, durationMs, artworkUrl, licenseReference, sourceLabel, allowedTerritories[], streamAllowed, offlineAllowed, rightsConfirmed, assetRef, version`
+   - `artists/{artistId}`: `name, city, genre, bio, provenanceBadge, rightsConfirmed, youtubeChannelUrl?`
+   - `playlists/{curatedId}`: `title, kind (shelf/editorial), trackIds[], territory`
+2. **Binary audio store**: Cloud Storage bucket or signed-CDN origin; access only via short-lived signed URLs (TTL ≤ 6 h) issued by an owner-controlled endpoint. No public read objects. URLs must match an allowlisted exact host enforced by `LicensedCatalogRights.isTrustedHttpsMediaUrl`; allowlist changes require a code change + review (hosts are not self-asserted by tracks).
+3. **Rights record invariants** (mirror `LicensedCatalogTrack`):
+   - `rightsConfirmed = true` ONLY when an authenticated agreement record exists; demo fixtures keep `DEMO-*` references and `isDemo = true`.
+   - `licenseExpiresAtEpochMs` enforced by `evaluate(..., CatalogAccess.STREAM / SAVE_OFFLINE / PLAY_DOWNLOADED)`.
+   - Territory `NG` default; `GH` allowed where agreement covers; unknown territory → deny.
+4. **Client pipeline**:
+   - Fetch metadata over HTTPS/TLS only; cache locally with bounded size + TTL ≤ 24 h (consistent with ADR-001 YouTube cache discipline); offline reads serve cache; missing network never claims rights it does not have.
+   - Downloads remain Media3 `DownloadManager` + `OfflineReadinessVerifier`; "Ready offline" requires completed bytes in `DownloadIndex`, never a metadata flag.
+   - No analytics/ad SDK in the MVP data path; no user-library upload.
+5. **Security & policy**:
+   - No YouTube/`googlevideo.com` assets in the catalog; those hosts never enter `trustedMediaHosts`.
+   - Signed URL rotation on compromise; client stores no long-lived credentials; API key (if any) server-side only.
+6. **Offline-first degradation**: backend unreachable → existing demo catalog labeled DEMO remains playable; UI shows "Licensed catalogue offline — showing demos"; no fabricated `LICENSED` badges.
+
+## Acceptance tests for the future backend source
+
+- `LicensedCatalogBackendSource` returns zero tracks when no valid agreement (fail-closed test).
+- Every returned track passes `LicensedCatalogRights.evaluate(track, STREAM, "NG")`; a tampered record (blank `licenseReference`, non-allowlisted host, expired license) evaluates to deny with the expected `CatalogDenial`.
+- Signed URL expiry honored; a cached track whose license expired denies `PLAY_DOWNLOADED` until re-verified.
+- Demo and licensed sets never mix labels in one track record.
+
+## Integration order (owner-approved roadmap)
+
+1. Contract review + rights policy (legal agreement templates for independent artists via Creator Hub form).
+2. Backend minimal: one track, one artist, signed URL, gate tests green.
+3. Editorials/shelves feeding `HomeFeedScreen` Phase B templates.
+4. Offline download rights per track; eviction policy for cache.
