+# Phase D — approval-gated proposal (apply nothing without a written owner decision)
+
+Phase D changes build configuration, dependencies, permissions, or release tooling. The sandbox
+and the agent must not apply these snippets. Each row records the snippet, the approval wording the
+owner must send, and the evidence that must exist before merging. Existing snippets live under
+`assets/templates/config/`; read the matching file before editing any real Gradle/Manifest file.
+
+## Gate table
+
+| # | Item | Snippet file | Required owner approval (verbatim in PR) | Mandatory evidence after apply | Rollback |
+|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+| D1 | Room persistence for playlists (replace JSON store; keep `PlaylistStore` interface) | `config/libs.versions.snippet.toml` (`room 2.6.1`); `config/app-build.snippet.kts` (KSP + room runtime/compiler) | "Approve Room adoption for playlists; keep `PlaylistStore` seam; migrate JSON users, do not drop old file." | `:app:kspDebugKotlin` green; `PlaylistRepositoryTest` green; `assembleDebug`; device relaunch shows created playlists; migration test (old JSON → DB) recorded | Revert commit; JSON file remains; no destructive migration delete until migration test passes |
+| D2 | Album art images (choose one path) — (a) no-dep MediaStore `Albums.ALBUM_ART` loader; (b) Coil `coil-compose 2.7.0` | `config/libs.versions.snippet.toml` (`coil`); `config/app-build.snippet.kts` (`implementation(libs.coil.compose)`) | "Approve art path (a) MediaStore-only / (b) Coil; no new network image host." | Screenshots of Home + player art on emulator with media; `lintDebug`; no new permission; no network call in art loader | Remove composable call; delete dependency line |
+| D3 | `media3-ui 1.5.1` helpers (only if a `PlayerView`/compact controller replaces custom transport) | `config/libs.versions.snippet.toml` (`media3Ui`); `config/app-build.snippet.kts` | "Approve media3-ui; existing `LocalAudioPlaybackService` session and rights gate unchanged." | Device proof: background session persists, queue metadata correct; `LicensedCatalogPlaybackInstrumentedTest` green | Revert dependency; custom transport returns |
+| D4 | `POST_NOTIFICATIONS` permission (API 33+) | `config/manifest.snippet.xml` | "Approve notification permission after confirming Media3 posts a foreground notification on API 33+; add runtime request before first play." | On API 33 emulator: permission dialog shown once; notification appears while playing; deny still allows playback | Remove manifest line + request branch; service still runs without notification on lower APIs |
+| D5 | Release R8/minify (`isMinifyEnabled=true`, `isShrinkResources=true`, keep rules) | `config/app-build.snippet.kts` release block | "Approve R8 release build; signing keystore remains owner-managed; do not auto-sign." | `assembleRelease` (unsigned) green; proguard rules for media3/room/coil reviewed; debug unaffected | Flip flags back to `false`; no keystore changes allowed from this agent |
+| D6 | Licensed backend per `references/data-source-contract.md` (replace demo fixtures) | contract reference only | "Approve backend contract (Firestore metadata + signed CDN); demo fallback retained until rights signs off." | `LicensedCatalogRights.evaluate` tests for real records; no offline playable record without `offlineAllowed`; demo fixtures still labeled DEMO | Revert data source; demo seam returns |
+
+## Standing prohibitions in Phase D
+
+- No Hilt/Dagger, Ktor/Retrofit, Firebase, or analytics dependency unless listed above and approved.
+- No manifest permission beyond D4; no `INTERNET` change for local playback; no cleartext config.
+- No release keystore, `key.properties`, or signing-config edit from the agent; owner runs signing.
+- No deletion of the legacy SharedPreferences/JSON playlist file before the D1 migration test passes.
+- Enhanced player sheet swap (Patch 5) is not a Phase D item; it needs a C-phase device proof first.
+
+## Suggested approval packet to the owner
+
+1. Per-row decision (approve / defer / reject) with the verbatim wording from the table.
+2. Target device API for D4 and whether the foreground notification currently posts.
+3. Chosen art path D2(a) vs D2(b).
+4. Whether D5 waits until after a signed internal-test APK exists.
+5. Owner machine gate run (`./gradlew :app:testDebugUnitTest`, `:app:lintDebug`, `:app:assembleDebug`, instrumented test) recorded with labels.
